+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | In Progress          |
+
+`ToolRegistry.execute` validates caller-supplied `input` against the resolved tool definition's `inputSchema` before calling the tool executor, returning a rejection `ToolResponse` when validation fails so the AI model can read the failure and self-correct within the orchestrator's tool-round budget rather than terminating the stream with an unhandled exception.
+
+## Execution Contract
+
+- When `input` fails the tool's `inputSchema`, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names the missing required field and never invokes the executor ([validated by: rejects input missing a required field with a ToolResponse and never invokes the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L24)).
+- When a field has the wrong type, the rejection `ToolResponse` and any emitted log lines name the failing property path and expected type without including the offending property value ([validated by: rejects a wrong-typed field without echoing the offending value in the response or logs](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L40)).
+- Validation enforces declared constraints (`required`, `type`, `enum`) without injecting `additionalProperties: false`, coercing types, or applying defaults, so valid input carrying unlisted extra properties reaches the executor unchanged.
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` still throws `Unknown tool: <name>` when called with a tool name that has not been registered.
+- Inside `ChatOrchestrator`, a rejected tool call is returned to the provider as a `tool_result` message on the next round rather than rejecting `processMessage`, allowing the model to issue a corrected call within `maxToolRounds` ([validated by: feeds a rejected tool call back to the provider as a tool_result so the next round can recover](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L114)).
+
+## Schema Compilation and Caching
+
+- For a static `ToolDefinition`, `ToolRegistry.register` compiles `inputSchema` at registration time and throws an error naming the tool if the schema cannot be compiled ([validated by: throws at registration time for an uncompilable schema and names the tool](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L72)).
+- A static tool's schema is compiled once at registration time and reused across `execute` calls rather than recompiled on every invocation.
+- For a function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource`, `ToolRegistry.execute` resolves the definition on each call and validates against the schema returned for that call, caching compiled validators by the resolved schema object ([validated by: validates a function-valued tool definition against the schema returned on each call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L83)).
